Sends push notifications about system events to Telegram, Pushover, ntfy, Gotify, Discord, Slack, Matrix, email, webhooks and the many other services supported by Apprise. Channels are built from a service picker, or from an Apprise URL you enter yourself, and each channel chooses which events it receives.

Events: configuration changes (who changed what), logins and lockouts, gateway down and recovery (with outage duration), WAN address changes, interface link up and down, VPN peers connecting and disconnecting (WireGuard online, stale or offline, as on the dashboard), new devices on the network, intrusion detection alerts, Monit checks failing and recovering, a state table filling up, UPS power events from apcupsd or NUT, firmware updates, certificates nearing expiry, System Status notices, critical messages in the local logs, CARP state changes and firewall startup.

A channel can also get a daily, weekly or monthly summary: current status, the events it chose with their most frequent details, firewall blocks and traffic per interface, the block rules matched most, and system health. By email it is a formatted report with graphs and pie charts from the firewall's health data; other services get the headline figures with a link to the full report on the firewall. Sent summaries are kept in an archive.

Notifications that cannot be delivered, for example while the only WAN is down, are retried with a backoff for up to 24 hours.

